      // The pod is a wing-case shell, like the reference thrusters: a big, deep superellipsoid that narrows to a tip turned
      // in toward the spine, cut into armour plates (a violet cap, a cream band, a violet mid plate, a cream band and a violet
      // skirt). Each plate is its own group: the shell, bevelled by a chamfered cutter run up its height and sliced to its
      // band, each a step prouder than the plate above so they shingle. The dark rim shell beneath carries the swings,
      // shows through the seams and borders the plates' bevelled sides. The right pod mirrors it.
